Subject: libiris: do not order-compare QList::contains with zero

Qt4's QList::contains returns QBool, whose safe-bool conversion yields a
const void*, so "> 0" is an ordered pointer comparison. That was tolerated as
a warning in C++98 and is an error now; compare against the null pointer
constant instead, which keeps the meaning.
--- a/protocols/jabber/libiris/src/xmpp/xmpp-im/filetransfer.cpp
+++ b/protocols/jabber/libiris/src/xmpp/xmpp-im/filetransfer.cpp
@@ -430,7 +430,7 @@
 
 bool FileTransferManager::isActive(const FileTransfer *ft) const
 {
-	return d->list.contains(const_cast<FileTransfer*>(ft)) > 0;
+	return d->list.contains(const_cast<FileTransfer*>(ft)) != 0;
 }
 
 void FileTransferManager::setDisabled(const QString &ns, bool state)
